{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01218",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 5.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.17,
      "end_seconds": 9.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.9,
      "end_seconds": 13.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.33,
      "end_seconds": 22.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got pins and needles in my hands and feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.95,
      "end_seconds": 26.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.22,
      "end_seconds": 31.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I've had it for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.63,
      "end_seconds": 37.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.76,
      "end_seconds": 40.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "I'd call it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.8,
      "end_seconds": 43.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Have you been forgetting words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.54,
      "end_seconds": 48.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Yeah. About three months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.28,
      "end_seconds": 53.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Alright, has there been any loss of vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.9,
      "end_seconds": 58.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Not at all, no loss of vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.48,
      "end_seconds": 66.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Have you noticed rash, bladder problems, weight loss or weakness of one side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.28,
      "end_seconds": 78.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I haven't had rash, bladder problems, weight loss or weakness of one side, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.69,
      "end_seconds": 83.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.39,
      "end_seconds": 87.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.95,
      "end_seconds": 91.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.04,
      "end_seconds": 94.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.27,
      "end_seconds": 103.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Alright, what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.57,
      "end_seconds": 109.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.12,
      "end_seconds": 114.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Okay, do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.75,
      "end_seconds": 118.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.15,
      "end_seconds": 122.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.32,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.56,
      "end_seconds": 144.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.94,
      "end_seconds": 148.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.76,
      "end_seconds": 153.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.76,
      "end_seconds": 159.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Grass pollen. I come out in... well, sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.57,
      "end_seconds": 175.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Alright, what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.74,
      "end_seconds": 183.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "I'm on sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.48,
      "end_seconds": 188.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.96,
      "end_seconds": 191.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "For two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.69,
      "end_seconds": 206.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.26,
      "end_seconds": 209.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.33,
      "end_seconds": 215.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.85,
      "end_seconds": 226.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.38,
      "end_seconds": 256.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.6 degrees, blood pressure 118 over 77, respiratory rate 16. And pulse is 75 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.04,
      "end_seconds": 260.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.07,
      "end_seconds": 264.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.71,
      "end_seconds": 277.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "The tongue looks smooth and red."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.28,
      "end_seconds": 280.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.51,
      "end_seconds": 295.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Your vibration sense is reduced at the ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.19,
      "end_seconds": 334.53,
      "duration_seconds": 33.34,
      "text": "Right, please sit back down. I want a vitamin B12 level done, that's for tingling and tiredness. I'm sending you for a thyroid test because of tiredness. For this, cyanocobalamin, 1000 micrograms, every other day, for two weeks. It's for low vitamin B12. Eating more eggs, dairy and fortified cereals will help over time. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.27,
      "end_seconds": 337.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.58,
      "end_seconds": 344.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.77,
      "end_seconds": 355.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "So, I take the cyanocobalamin, 1000 micrograms, every other day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.87,
      "end_seconds": 361.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.54,
      "end_seconds": 366.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.85,
      "end_seconds": 368.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}